{"id":"w102205","name":"Dahi Baingana (Fried Eggplant in Yogurt)","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Dahi_Baingana_(Fried_Eggplant_in_Yogurt)"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Dahi_Baingana_(Fried_Eggplant_in_Yogurt)"},"image":"","cuisine":"Indian","country":"","region":"South Asia","course":"main","protein":"veggie","diet":2,"allergens":2,"minutes":55,"time":{"prep":20,"cook":30,"passive":5,"passiveWhy":["cooling"]},"timeEstimated":true,"servings":"","difficulty":"medium","ingredients":[{"item":"2 medium-sized bainganas (eggplant / brinjal / begun)","qty":""},{"item":"Oil","qty":""},{"item":"Panch puran (futana / Bengali five spice)","qty":""},{"item":"2 Indian red chiles (sukhila lanka)","qty":""},{"item":"10 curry leaves (kadi patta / bhersunga patra)","qty":""},{"item":"2 tbsp dahi (yogurt)","qty":""},{"item":"250 ml (1 cup) water","qty":""},{"item":"1 tbsp sugar","qty":""},{"item":"Salt","qty":""}],"steps":["Cut eggplant into thin slices, lengthwise. Deep fry in oil. Keep aside.","Mix dahi with water.","Heat 1 tbsp of oil in a pan. Add panch puran and red chili, then cook until the spices splutter.","Add dahi-water mix, salt to taste, and sugar. Stir properly and make a gravy.","Add fried eggplant to the gravy, and lower the flame.","Heat it for 2–3 minutes, then leave it to cool.","Serve with rice."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}